Under `--modular-termination`, a library may now refine a module that has opaque functions. A refinement copies the reveal lemmas that Dafny generates for them, and `dafny build --target:lib` refused the copies as members marked `{:verify false}`. The copies are now recognised as generated, like the lemmas they copy; a `{:verify false}` that the user writes is still refused. As a result, `Std.Strings`, whose conversion modules refine `Std.Arithmetic.LittleEndianNat`, joins the standard-library core that is built with `--modular-termination-trust:standard-library` (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/211), and that library's record now lists all 18 premises of the trust list (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/357).
